  "model": "Claude Fable 5.1 (Claude Code)",
  "construction": "Two-block group-algebra (2BGA) code over SmallGroup(64,47) = C16 : C4, archive row \"64 47 8 9 [ 3 ] [ 2, 15, 26 ]\" of the nonabelian enumeration (Lin and Pryadko, arXiv:2306.16400; github.com/QEC-pages/2BGA-codes @ 403d194c3f98). a = {g_i : i in [3]} and b = {g_i : i in [2, 15, 26]} with elements indexed as GAP's Elements(SmallGroup(64,47)) numbers them, 1-based (the identity is implicit in the archive's lists); H_X = [L(a) | R(b)], H_Z = [R(b)^T | L(a)^T] over the left and right regular representations. Rebuilt here as research/kit/group_algebra.build_2bga_small_group(64, 47, [0, 2], [0, 1, 14, 25]) on the committed Cayley table research/kit/groups/smallgroup_64_47.json (GAP 4.16.1, smallgrp 1.7.0), 0-based indices with the identity at 0.",
  "references": [
   "arXiv:2306.16400",
   "https://github.com/QEC-pages/2BGA-codes"
  ],
  "date": "2023",
  "notes": "Literature baseline (arXiv:2306.16400, Lin and Pryadko, 28 Jun 2023), seeded for issue #3658 as the 2BGA archive row that dominates 128-8-6 at equal n, k, and check weight. Reconstructed here from the archive row with the group table exported by research/kit/groups/cayley_table.g; n, k, and the check weight match the row, and the reconstruction convention was checked by rebuilding five archive rows already on the board and finding each permutation-equivalent to its entry. The archive's d = 9 is a QDistRnd upper bound; this entry claims d <= 9 from its own witnesses (40,000 RIS trials per side on the NumPy backend, seed 20261017, X 9, Z 9), and 2 x 2,000,000 gf2_fast trials found nothing lighter than 9.",
